translated_text:
Article 24
(1) Forms of violence against Women include: a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. domestic neglect;
e. trafficking of women; and
f. exploitation.
(2) Implementation of protection for women victims of violence in order to provide legal protection and/or health recovery (3) Protection for women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
a. legal assistance;
b. assistance following the occurrence of acts of violence; c. rehabilitation and social reintegration; and
d. health services.

text:
Pasal 26
(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggungjawab  terhadap pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan. (2) Upaya pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), meliputi :
a. penetapan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan;
b. penetapan pedoman pelaksanaan;
c. penyelenggaraan layanan; dan
d. koordinasi kebijakan, program dan kegiatan.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 14 (3) Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 25 huruf a meliputi: a. melaksanakan kebijakan Perlindungan Perempuan dari segala bentuk diskriminasi dan tindak kekerasan; b. menetapkan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan  Pemberdayaan dan Perlindungan Perempuan yang telah  ditetapkan;
c. mengumpulkan data dan informasi tentang Perempuan  Korban Kekerasan dan Diskriminasi serta peraturan  perundang-undangan pendukungnya;
d. melakukan pendidikan tentang hal yang berkaitan  dengan Perlindungan Perempuan Korban Kekerasan  dan Diskriminasi;
e. melakukan sosialisasi peraturan perundang-undangan  yang berkaitan dengan Perlindungan Perempuan  Korban Kekerasan dan Diskriminasi;
f. melakukan pemantauan dan evaluasi terhadap  penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Perempuan Korban  Kekerasan dan Diskriminasi.
(4) Untuk mengantisipasi terjadinya tindak Kekerasan,  Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyediakan dan  menyelenggarakan pelayanan bagi Korban dalam bentuk: a. mendirikan dan memfasilitasi terselenggaranya lembaga layanan terpadu untuk Korban dengan melibatkan  unsur masyarakat;
b. memfasilitasi pendampingan bantuan hukum dan pelayanan hukum sesuai kebutuhan Korban;
c. menyediakan rumah aman atau tempat tinggal  alternatif beserta mekanisme penanganan, pelayanan,  psikososial dan spiritual;
d. melakukan penanganan berkelanjutan sampai pada  tahap rehabilitasi dan reintegrasi sosial;
e. melakukan pemantauan dan eveluasi terhadap  penyelenggaraan perlindungan Korban; dan
f. mendorong kepedulian masyarakat akan pentingnya  Perlindungan terhadap Korban.
(5) Dalam melaksanakan kewajiban sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (3) dan ayat (4) Pemerintah Daerah wajib  memperhatikan hak dan kewajiban Orang Tua, wali, suami  atau orang lain yang secara hukum bertanggungjawab  terhadap Korban.
(6) Untuk melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawab  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) sampai dengan ayat  (4) Pemerintah Daerah menyusun rencana aksi daerah  Perlindungan tehadap Perempuan Korban Kekerasan.
(7) Ketentuan mengenai rencana aksi daerah Perlindungan  tehadap Perempuan Korban Kekerasan sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (6) diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 15

translated_text:
Article 26
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility for the empowerment and protection of women. (2) The efforts for empowerment and protection of women as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
a. determination of policies, programs, and activities;
b. determination of implementation guidelines;
c. provision of services; and
d. coordination of policies, programs and activities.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 14 (3) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 25 letter a include: a. implementing policies for the Protection of Women from all forms of discrimination and acts of violence; b. determining policies, programs, and activities for the Empowerment and Protection of Women that have been established;
c. collecting data and information about Women Victims of Violence and Discrimination as well as supporting laws and regulations;
d. conducting education on matters related to the Protection of Women Victims of Violence and Discrimination;
e. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the Protection of Women Victims of Violence and Discrimination;
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of Protection of Women Victims of Violence and Discrimination.
(4) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of Violence, the Regional Government is obliged to provide and organize services for Victims in the form of: a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for Victims by involving community elements;
b. facilitating legal aid assistance and legal services according to the needs of Victims;
c. providing safe houses or alternative residences along with handling mechanisms, psychosocial and spiritual services;
d. conducting continuous handling up to the rehabilitation and social reintegration stage;
e. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of Victims; and
f. encouraging public awareness of the importance of Protection for Victims.
(5) In carrying out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (3) and paragraph (4), the Regional Government must pay attention to the rights and obligations of Parents, guardians, husbands or other persons who are legally responsible for the Victim.
(6) To carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) through paragraph (4), the Regional Government shall prepare a regional action plan for the Protection of Women Victims of Violence.
(7) Provisions regarding the regional action plan for the Protection of Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (6) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 15

text:
Pasal 28
(1) Bupati melaksanakan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan  Perlindungan Perempuan untuk menghapus segala bentuk  diskriminasi dan tindak Kekerasan Terhadap Perempuan.
(2) Perangkat Daerah membidangi Perempuan melaksanakan  kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan Perlindungan Perempuan  yang telah ditetapkan dan pelaksanaannya berkerjasama  dan berkoordinasi dengan Perangkat Daerah terkait,  penegak hukum, lembaga masyarakat, perguruan tinggi,  dan masyarakat.
(3) Pelaksanaan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan  Perlindungan Perempuan sebagaimana pada ayat (2)  berupa:
a. analisis kebijakan;
b. advokasi;
c. koordinasi dan komunikasi;
d. sosialisasi;
e. edukasi;
f. pelatihan;
g. fasilitasi;
h. penyediaan pelayanan; dan
i. bentuk lainnya.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 16

translated_text:
Article 28
(1) The Regent implements policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of Violence Against Women.
(2) Regional Apparatus with responsibility for Women implements policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women that have been established and their implementation is carried out in cooperation and coordination with relevant Regional Apparatus, law enforcement, community institutions, universities, and the community.
(3) The implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be in the form of:
a. policy analysis;
b. advocacy;
c. coordination and communication;
d. socialization;
e. education;
f. training;
g. facilitation;
h. provision of services; and
i. other forms.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 16

Article 29
(1) The Regent in implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women as referred to in Article 28 shall undertake efforts to:
a. coordinate implementation among Regional Apparatus;
b. cooperate with the central government, provincial government, and other regency/city governments in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. strengthen the capacity of gender institutions;
d. facilitate services for the Protection of Women;
e. provide services for the Protection of Women;
f. implement affirmative action for the Protection of Women; and
g. compile a data system for the Protection of Women including a data system for Violence Against Women.
(2) The implementation of policies, programs, and activities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be coordinated by the Vice Regent.

